Package: SuSiEOut
Type: Package
Title: SuSiE-OUT Fine-Mapping with Expanded Variant References
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Josh", "Weinstock", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "josh.weinstock@emory.edu")
Author: Josh Weinstock [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Josh Weinstock <josh.weinstock@emory.edu>
Description: Implements SuSiE-OUT, a sparse summary-statistic fine-mapping
    model with L-invariant locus-level effect-count priors. A sparse effect can
    be null, caused by a tested
    variant, or caused by a variant outside the tested set that is represented
    through its linkage disequilibrium pattern in an expanded whole-genome
    sequencing panel.
    Rank-one Bayes factors integrate normal-mixture effect priors, while
    infinitesimal and linkage-disequilibrium mismatch covariance terms provide
    explicit competing explanations for diffuse signal and reference error.
